    "verdict": "NULL \u2014 no detectable announcement effect on semiconductor sector RV in the T+1..+5 window after CHIPS Act award/delay events. Aggregate post/pre ratio = 0.950, sign test p=0.997, 0/146 per-event tests significant after Bonferroni. LOW POWER CAVEAT: N=17 events x 12 tickers => only 146 per-event tests; the random-anchor null is conservative (uses full sample including the event window itself as anchors), and Bonferroni at alpha=0.05/146 is extremely strict. A genuine moderate-size effect (ratio ~1.2-1.5) is detectable only if highly clustered; diffuse or heterogeneous announcement effects would also produce this NULL. Interpret as 'no strong, concentrated, systematically positive RV spike', not 'no effect at all'.",
